	{
		uid: "3e6350d7",
		type: "item",
		item: {
			id: "ironchest:iron_chest",
			Damage: 5s,
			tag: {
				BlockEntityTag: {
					facing: 3b,
					Lock: "",
					id: "minecraft:ironchest.crystal",
					Items: [{
						Damage: 0s,
						Slot: 0b,
						id: "mca:book_death",
						Count: 1b,
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"I couldn't count how many times my family has been blown to pieces by creepers.How are they still around, you may ask?Easy! I, dear reader, have discovered a CURE for death itself! And through this book, I can share it with you.",
								"§lStaff Of Life§rThe Staff is a powerful item that can revive up to 5 people. Wave the staff around and speak the name of the villager you wish to revive. Within moments, your loved one will be fully revived!",
								"§lSummoning Grim§rUnfortunately, you must obtain the Staff from the Grim Reaper himself.To summon him, you must build an altar consisting of 3 obsidian columns that are at least 2 blocks high. They may be higher if you like.",
								"§lSummoning Grim pt. 2§r     # # # X # # ## # # # # # ## # # # # # #X # # E # # XX = Obsidian ColumnE = Emerald# = Empty",
								"§lSummoning Grim pt. 3§rAfter building the altar, wait until night and light all 3 columns.When you're ready to fight, light the emerald block and run!",
								"§lFighting Grim§rGrim is tough. Use full diamond armor, lots of potions, and lots of enchantments.He can:- Fly- Block attacks- Blind you- Move your items- Teleport",
								"§lFighting Grim pt. 2§rIf you hit Grim while he's blocking, he will teleport behind you and strike.Do not try to use arrows or poison, he is immune!",
								"§lFighting Grim pt. 3§rWhen Grim is at §lhalf health§r he will teleport into the air and begin healing.While healing, he will summon his minions from the underworld to fight you.",
								"§lFighting Grim pt. 4§rWhen Grim is healed, he will continue attacking you, but he won't be able to heal again for 3 minutes and 30 seconds.Each time Grim heals, he will not be able to restore as much health has he did previously."
							],
							resolved: 1b,
							title: "死亡，以及如何治愈它！",
							author: "Ozzie the Warrior"
						}
					},
					{
						Damage: 0s,
						Slot: 1b,
						id: "mca:book_romance",
						Count: 1b,
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"§lIntroduction§rInteraction is key to building relationships and finding the love of your life.I've happily written this book in order to share my knowledge of interaction, love, and, unfortunately, divorce, to anyone who may need a little push in the right direction.",
								"§lInteracting§rChoose wisely when interacting with a villager!If choosing a romantic interaction, be sure that the villager you are talking to likes you a lot.",
								"§lInteracting pt. 2§rDon't be annoying! Talking to someone for too long will bore them, and your interactions may stop succeeding.If this happens, simply wait a few minutes before trying to talk to them again.",
								"§lMarriage§rTo get married, simply gift a villager a wedding ring once you feel you have reached the highest relationship level.Once you're married, you can then procreate and have children of your own!"
							],
							resolved: 1b,
							title: "人际关系与你的故事",
							author: "Gerry the Librarian"
						}
					},
					{
						Damage: 0s,
						Slot: 2b,
						id: "mca:book_family",
						Count: 1b,
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"Children are our future! Make sure to have as many as you possibly can.Not only do you get to experience the joy of raising a child, but once they are past the baby stage, put them to work!",
								"§lBabies§rWhen you are married, simply approach your spouse and offer to 'Procreate'.After a short dance, you'll be the proud owner of a new baby boy or girl (or maybe even both)!",
								"§lGrowth§rBabies take time to grow, make sure to hold them until they are ready, or give them to your spouse to take care of.Once a baby is ready to grow, you may place it on the ground and it will grow into a child!",
								"§lAdolescence§rChildren will grow slowly from a baby to a teen.However, the magical properties of Golden Apples are said to accelerate any child's growth. I have yet to try this myself.",
								"§lChores§rAny child can harvest, chop wood, prospect, hunt, and fish. You'll need to provide them with the tools they need to do so.If a tool breaks and the child doesn't have another, they will have no choice but to stop working.",
								"§lAdulthood§rAs sad as it may be, children will eventually grow into adults.Adults can be married off by using Matchmaker's Rings, or they will eventually get married on their own."
							],
							resolved: 1b,
							title: "管理你的家庭 第11卷",
							author: "Leanne the Cleric"
						}
					},
					{
						Damage: 0s,
						Slot: 3b,
						id: "mca:book_rose_gold",
						Count: 1b,
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"§lWarning!TOP SECRET§rThis manual is the property of William Mining Co.If you are not a William Mining Co. employee, please refrain from reading this manual and return promptly to William the Miner.",
								"Ah, rose gold - a lovely combination of silver, copper, and gold that smelts into a pinkish orange metal.Most use it as an alternative to gold for crafting rings as it is much less expensive.However, it has some interesting qualities that are easy to miss.",
								"§lCreating Dust§rRose gold, once smelted, can be crushed into a fine dust.Look closely at rose gold dust in bright light, and you'll see shiny flecks of pure gold!",
								"§lWashing Dust§rWith a little work, we can actually extract the gold from the dust and create pure gold ingots. Simply mix dust with a bucket of water.The lighter silver and copper components will wash away, leaving you with about 6 smaller piles of gold dust.",
								"§lExtracting Gold§rArrange 9 piles of dust on your crafting table, and if you're lucky, you'll find a gold nugget in one of them!And of course, once you have 9 gold nuggets, you'll be able to craft them into a solid gold ingot."
							],
							resolved: 1b,
							title: "玫瑰金之上",
							author: "William the Miner"
						}
					},
					{
						Damage: 0s,
						Slot: 4b,
						id: "mca:book_infection",
						Count: 1b,
						tag: {
							pages: [
								"Good day, readers! I've written this book so that you may not end up suffering the same fate as I.Although I caught the infection, I was luckily able to keep all of my mental faculties.",
								"§lWhat is the Infection?§rI discovered long ago that the zombies that appear at night are actually villagers in the late stages of infection!Newly infected villagers turn green, are unable to speak, and occasionally try to bite!",
								"§lCuring§rContrary to popular belief, the infection can be cured if caught in time.You must first weaken the villager or zombie with a potion.Then, immediately feed them a golden apple.",
								"§lCuring pt. 2§rZombies that can be cured often have enlarged heads and noses.Any other zombies you see unfortunately are too far gone, and cannot be cured.",
								"§lCuring pt. 3§rZombies will take a couple of minutes to be fully cured.Villagers who were recently infected, though, and haven't had time to degrade into a full zombie, will be cured instantly!",
								"§lWarnings§rVillagers are highly susceptible to infection, and children even more so!If you carry a baby with you while fighting zombies, there is a chance it can become infected."
							],
							resolved: 1b,
							title: "小心感染！",
							author: "Richard the Zombie"
						}
					}]
